WEBVTT

01:42.880 --> 01:43.970
He's fast!

01:47.790 --> 01:50.090
Faster than anyone I've fought before.

02:04.060 --> 02:06.520
And that sword...

02:07.120 --> 02:09.710
He uses the curve of the blade.

02:09.710 --> 02:12.210
He's handling a dagger's range well, too.

02:14.310 --> 02:17.490
Are you serious? He's unarmed.

02:18.630 --> 02:21.480
I'm a warrior of Miklagard.

02:25.760 --> 02:29.380
He hasn't experienced
a single good thing, huh?

02:27.290 --> 02:32.290
The Road Home

02:31.150 --> 02:32.360
No kidding.

02:32.770 --> 02:37.010
What kind of monsters surrounded him?

02:52.190 --> 02:53.770
I'll overwhelm him with a flurry of blows.

02:58.530 --> 03:00.020
Dodge this!

03:15.270 --> 03:16.420
He's strong.

03:18.260 --> 03:22.280
What's a warrior this skilled doing
defending a farm?

03:22.800 --> 03:26.290
How'd a man this skilled end up a slave?

03:27.710 --> 03:30.040
No, don't get worked up.

03:30.040 --> 03:32.470
Don't follow his lead.

03:34.080 --> 03:35.410
The important thing is...

03:47.710 --> 03:49.320
He can strike even faster?

03:51.110 --> 03:52.080
But...

03:53.940 --> 03:54.980
I see it.

04:10.450 --> 04:11.880
He got me.

04:13.230 --> 04:14.790
He's next to Gardar...

04:37.390 --> 04:37.990
Snake!

04:37.990 --> 04:39.170
Please don't, Mister Snake!

04:43.430 --> 04:47.460
Please don't kill Gardar.

04:49.430 --> 04:53.090
Please let this go.

05:00.950 --> 05:04.330
Don't be so self-centered, Arnheid.

05:05.470 --> 05:08.870
He killed five of my men.

05:08.870 --> 05:10.650
I can't overlook that.

05:11.580 --> 05:18.200
Snake! I'll do whatever I can to express
my condolences for the loss of your men.

05:18.200 --> 05:20.140
I'll even sell my farm to—

05:20.140 --> 05:23.480
Shut up, Gramps! This isn't about money!

05:27.160 --> 05:33.600
Both me and my men are a
bunch of stupid, nasty scumbags.

05:34.070 --> 05:39.600
We're drifters who can't use our real names
because of what we've done elsewhere.

05:40.010 --> 05:43.590
But does that mean
it doesn't matter if we die, huh?

05:44.600 --> 05:47.790
Is Gardar's life worth that much?

05:47.790 --> 05:49.990
More than the lives of five of my men?

05:50.520 --> 05:53.990
Tell me, Thorfinn! Arnheid!

05:54.470 --> 05:56.770
Tell me how much more he's worth.

06:06.690 --> 06:09.850
They're not that different, huh?

06:11.270 --> 06:12.640
In that case...

06:12.640 --> 06:13.450
Don't—

06:14.110 --> 06:16.170
The cost of life...

06:16.890 --> 06:19.890
...can only be paid with life!

07:05.310 --> 07:07.000
You still want to fight?

07:08.900 --> 07:12.580
Will you avenge Gardar?

07:17.630 --> 07:21.430
Arnheid, you're the one who
cut Gardar's bonds, aren't you?

07:23.350 --> 07:26.410
You two will be punished accordingly.

07:27.630 --> 07:30.630
Until the master returns, you'll be bound—

08:00.950 --> 08:03.790
Enough, Gardar!

08:07.490 --> 08:09.800
If you keep choking him, he'll die!

08:10.290 --> 08:11.800
Gardar!

08:12.190 --> 08:14.500
Damn! He's so strong...

08:19.890 --> 08:21.270
Gardar!

08:24.310 --> 08:25.690
Let go!

08:28.190 --> 08:29.560
Gardar!

08:40.470 --> 08:41.650
Gardar.

08:44.080 --> 08:46.760
Let's go home, Gardar.

08:55.490 --> 08:57.250
That's enough.

08:58.290 --> 09:02.100
There's no one to get in our way anymore.

09:03.030 --> 09:05.510
Hjalti is waiting for us.

09:32.080 --> 09:33.530
Hjalti...

09:36.740 --> 09:41.850
Where is he now?

09:56.580 --> 10:00.810
He's with your brother in Birka.

10:01.350 --> 10:04.710
I sent him to safety
before the fighting started.

10:06.880 --> 10:12.630
I see. My brother's always
done so much for me.

10:13.300 --> 10:18.870
I'll need to bring something to thank him
when we go to get Hjalti.

10:21.830 --> 10:24.360
You there...

10:25.760 --> 10:29.090
Is this your cart?

10:29.690 --> 10:31.240
I'd like to borrow it.

10:31.240 --> 10:33.000
Uh, actually...

10:33.600 --> 10:35.360
It's mine.

10:36.560 --> 10:40.250
You can have it, Gardar.

10:41.310 --> 10:42.360
Ah!

10:46.390 --> 10:49.200
Sorry for talking down to you from up here.

10:49.200 --> 10:51.720
Old man, what's your name?

10:53.070 --> 10:55.000
It's Sverkel.

10:56.210 --> 10:59.860
Go on. Return to your home.

11:01.300 --> 11:04.580
Thank you, Mister Sverkel.

11:11.910 --> 11:13.170
Thorfinn...

11:14.820 --> 11:16.260
And Einar.

11:16.710 --> 11:20.970
I can't thank you enough.

11:22.230 --> 11:24.780
This is reckless, Arnheid.

11:25.520 --> 11:28.460
Gardar is already...

11:35.680 --> 11:36.790
It's fine.

11:42.590 --> 11:44.340
Please send us off.

12:32.030 --> 12:33.700
I feel cold...

12:35.680 --> 12:39.030
Cold to my core.

12:52.660 --> 12:53.970
How miserable.

12:55.670 --> 13:00.970
Such unfortunate men, abandoned by the gods.

14:12.750 --> 14:14.360
You...

14:16.550 --> 14:19.380
You are my new pride.

14:20.800 --> 14:22.040
Hjalti...

14:22.640 --> 14:25.220
Hjalti, son of Gardar.

14:27.040 --> 14:29.210
Father shall fight for you.

14:30.110 --> 14:32.980
For honor, so you can be proud of him.

14:33.950 --> 14:37.100
For wealth that will someday be yours.

15:39.660 --> 15:40.980
Wait!

17:02.050 --> 17:05.940
For honor and wealth...

17:08.960 --> 17:10.250
Gardar?

17:17.620 --> 17:22.100
How old is Hjalti now?

17:23.780 --> 17:27.000
Eight? Nine?

17:31.190 --> 17:32.490
He's six.

17:33.450 --> 17:37.060
Ah, forgive me.

17:37.570 --> 17:41.570
I lost track of time since being enslaved.

17:43.140 --> 17:48.050
Six. I see. That's a shame.

17:49.060 --> 17:52.590
I missed his cute years.

17:54.000 --> 17:57.380
He was still only one when I last saw him.

17:59.950 --> 18:06.390
Good grief. He's probably forgotten about us.

18:09.970 --> 18:16.100
He's my son. He's surely
grown into a prankster.

18:16.880 --> 18:19.740
I bet he lights horses' tails on fire.

18:21.510 --> 18:25.490
You did that as a child?

18:26.030 --> 18:29.800
Yeah. I got in a lot of
trouble with my father.

18:36.400 --> 18:42.500
Once he's old enough, he'll probably say
he wants to go adventuring.

18:43.010 --> 18:44.630
All boys do.

18:49.970 --> 18:53.020
But I won't allow it.

19:08.510 --> 19:09.610
Gardar.

19:25.730 --> 19:31.330
I'm all right. I'm just a little tired.

19:33.520 --> 19:35.350
Let me rest.

20:17.360 --> 20:19.750
We're really doing this?

20:19.750 --> 20:22.860
Yeah. We've made up our minds.

20:22.860 --> 20:26.840
The villagers' lives will be easier
if we acquire iron.

20:26.840 --> 20:28.360
So will your family's.

20:34.080 --> 20:36.110
Fine. Let's go.

20:36.110 --> 20:36.670
All right.

20:39.190 --> 20:41.770
Everyone's already gathered in the square.

20:41.770 --> 20:43.380
Hurry.

21:08.870 --> 21:10.450
Arnheid...

21:12.640 --> 21:14.070
Hjalti...

21:17.270 --> 21:27.270
I'll never leave your sides again.

23:15.680 --> 23:25.400
I'm home.

23:38.290 --> 23:39.510
Welcome home.

23:41.920 --> 23:47.350
Welcome home, Gardar.

25:37.260 --> 25:40.220
The First Method

25:37.750 --> 25:39.480
"The First Method."
